+save/restore**, 23.8 % are structural (alloca/address/wide/nongpr) and only
+**10.7 % are spills** — and `sha256_transform`, the RA-PRESSURE-3 target, has
+**zero** spill references (5 alloca for `m[64]`, 12 csave). Backlog: RA-CSAVE-1
+opens the callee-save question; RA-GLA-04's Phase-2 remat prerequisite is
+satisfied and the item is now bounded to spill-dominated functions.
+
+### Linker suite: oracle-conformance predicate was rejecting a conforming lccc
+`reloc_pc32_out_of_range_diagnosed_{exec,script}_path` demanded the literal
+word "truncated" in every ORACLE's stderr, which is bfd's spelling; mold and
+lld say "out of range". Merely installing mold therefore flipped two passing
+tests to "lccc is inventing a restriction" — with no diagnostics printed, so
+the cause was invisible. The predicate now classifies each oracle as
